From 061c733e85dfeb1b2e305f3ec16279968dbd5de8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:00:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: the two views of a 3D Blu-ray are decoded from a
 disc too

The label of videoplayer.hades3dmvc said "in MKV files" and its help
said that a disc, an image of one or a folder of one still plays in 2D.
A disc gives both views now (the demuxer of the two clips of a 3D disc
and what tells it when to read the second one), so the label names no
container and the help names the disc first. In English and in the three
Spanish files of the skin, with the English text of each kept in step.
---
 addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po       | 4 ++--
 .../language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po           | 4 ++--
 .../language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po           | 8 ++++----
 .../language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po           | 8 ++++----
 .../language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po           | 8 ++++----
 5 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index d849a29..efa92cf 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -25223,13 +25223,13 @@ msgstr ""
 #. Hades: label of setting "videoplayer.hades3dmvc"; translated in Estuary (#31721)
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#39960"
-msgid "Decode both views of 3D Blu-ray video in MKV files (MVC)"
+msgid "Decode both views of 3D Blu-ray video (MVC)"
 msgstr ""
 
 #. Hades: help of setting "videoplayer.hades3dmvc"; translated in Estuary (#31722)
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#39961"
-msgid "A 3D Blu-ray holds the picture of each eye as a view of its own (H.264 MVC). Hades decodes both from a Matroska (MKV) file made of such a disc; a disc, an image of one or a folder of one still plays in 2D. Automatic: both views are decoded, by the processor, where the display says that it takes 3D (it has to be on when Hades starts), and the video is then shown as a stereoscopic one; on any other display the video plays in 2D as before, with hardware decoding. Always: both views on any display, for anaglyph glasses or for a 3D display that does not say what it is. Off: never. Where the second view cannot be decoded the video plays in 2D. Applies from the next video."
+msgid "A 3D Blu-ray holds the picture of each eye as a view of its own (H.264 MVC). Hades decodes both from a disc, an image of one or a folder of one, and from a Matroska (MKV) file made of such a disc. Automatic: both views are decoded, by the processor, where the display says that it takes 3D (it has to be on when Hades starts), and the video is then shown as a stereoscopic one; on any other display the video plays in 2D as before, with hardware decoding. Always: both views on any display, for anaglyph glasses or for a 3D display that does not say what it is. Off: never. Where the second view cannot be decoded the video plays in 2D. Applies from the next video."
 msgstr ""
 
